/backups

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# real-person profile packets for the manual provider (Law 5 hygiene)
/profiles

# Durability export (npm run state:export).
# The census is person-free and COMMITTED — it is the tripwire that makes data
# loss loud. The snapshot is person-linked (handles, bios, captions, DM text)
# and never enters git history, because Law 5 promises "trivial
# delete-on-request" and deleting from git history is not trivial. It leaves
# the container by being handed to the operator.
/state/snapshot.json

# Calibration run artifact (npm run calibrate). Person-linked — handles, names
# and per-candidate reasoning — so it follows snapshot.json out of git history
# for the same Law 5 reason: delete-on-request must stay trivial.
/state/calibration/
